WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.230
Netflix's October line-up is bursting with
gory goodness to usher in Halloween.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.419
But the streaming workhorse isn't a one-trick
pony, so you can also fill up on brand new

00:00:08.419 --> 00:00:13.330
comedy, action, drama, and new seasons of
your favorite TV shows, including the hotly

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.969
anticipated Stranger Things season two.

00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:19.410
Here's everything coming to Netflix in October
2017.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.759
Rodney Carrington: Here Comes the Truth

00:00:21.759 --> 00:00:26.070
Musician-comedian Rodney Carrington has made
a name for himself through his crude stand-up

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:30.349
infused with country music ballads, and he's
been touring again in summer 2017 with his

00:00:30.349 --> 00:00:32.820
brand new routine, Here Comes the Truth.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.810
If you haven't been able to see Carrington's
show live, it's coming as a Netflix exclusive

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.330
on October 3.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.540
The Bonus Family: Season 1

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.580
This popular Swedish series was earmarked
for global distribution by Netflix in early

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:50.440
2017 and rebranded as a Netflix original everywhere
outside of Sweden, marking another fantastic

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.370
foreign acquisition that, let's be honest,
nobody else would ever have heard of if not

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.450
for the streaming service.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:01.100
The dramedy series centers on four divorcees
who find new spouses...and new step-children.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.110
Only, in Sweden, step-mothers and step-fathers
are actually called "bonus moms" and "bonus

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.110
dads."

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.250
Netflix picked up distribution rights for
the first two seasons, so while only the first

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:14.080
season is dropping on October 5, chances are
you'll be able to find the second season on

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.310
Netflix sometime soon afterward.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.020
The Death and Life of Marsha P. Johnson

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:23.030
For those who don't know, Marsha P. Johnson
was an activist and transgender woman who

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.840
was an instrumental figure in the gay rights
movement for decades.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:31.130
On July 6, 1992, her body was found floating
in the Hudson River, sparking one of the most

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.000
hotly debated investigations in recent history.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.260
Although police initially ruled Johnson's
death a suicide, public outcry and a steadily

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:43.120
mounting pile of evidence forced police to
reopen her case in 2012 to determine if she

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.930
had, in reality, been murdered and dumped
in the river.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:50.120
The new Netflix documentary The Death and
Life of Marsha P. Johnson takes a hard look

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.799
at that investigation and the circumstances
leading up to Johnson's untimely death.

00:01:54.799 --> 00:01:56.880
Queue it up on October 6.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.869
Suburra Season 1

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:02.950
This crime thriller marks Netflix's first
Italian-language original series, but don't

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:06.820
let the subtitles hold you back — this series
looks to be packed with criminal intrigue,

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.749
political corruption, and all the dirty laundry
you'd expect from a mob story set in the heart

00:02:10.749 --> 00:02:11.749
of Rome.

00:02:11.749 --> 00:02:15.910
The series will serve as a prequel to the
2015 film of the same name, and if it's anywhere

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.120
near as good as that movie, Suburra may become
a modern crime classic.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.540
Plus, because it's a prequel, it's a safe
bet that viewers will be able to jump in even

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.989
if they haven't seen the movie.

00:02:25.989 --> 00:02:28.329
The first season drops October 6.

00:02:28.329 --> 00:02:30.569
Christina P: Mother Inferior

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:34.720
Comedian Christina Pazsitzky has been making
waves in the stand-up scene lately, although

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.069
she's still probably best known for her podcast,
Your Mom's House.

00:02:38.069 --> 00:02:42.740
Hopefully, her Netflix stand-up special Mother
Inferior, which premieres on October 10, will

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:46.349
change that and introduce Pazsitzky to a wider
audience.

00:02:46.349 --> 00:02:47.980
Fe de Etarras

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.499
October seems to be the month for foreign-language
originals.

00:02:50.499 --> 00:02:55.450
In addition to Suburra, Netflix is premiering
Fe de Etarras, a Spanish comedy film about

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:59.900
an unlikely group of people stuck in an apartment
waiting for a mysterious phone call.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.930
That's about as vague of a premise as you're
likely to find, but if you're in the mood

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:07.239
for something a little outside the box, you
can queue up Fe de Etarras when it hits Netflix

00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:09.500
worldwide on October 12.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.879
Kingdom of Us

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:15.579
Take a step inside small-town America with
Kingdom of Us, a poignant documentary chronicling

00:03:15.579 --> 00:03:19.849
the shattered lives of seven siblings whose
world was torn apart when their father committed

00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:20.849
suicide.

00:03:20.849 --> 00:03:24.559
Through candid interviews and home videos,
Kingdom of Us pieces together the bond this

00:03:24.559 --> 00:03:28.139
family shared with their father and the long
road ahead of them as they try to deal with

00:03:28.139 --> 00:03:29.779
the tragedy of his loss.

00:03:29.779 --> 00:03:34.640
It's guaranteed to be an emotional, painful
ride, but there may just be hope on the horizon.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.430
Experience all the highs and lows alongside
the Shanks family on October 13.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.590
Mindhunter: Season 1

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:45.450
From creator Joe Penhall, Mindhunter is an
all-new Netflix original that follows FBI

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:50.510
profiler Holden Ford, played by Jonathan Groff,
as he gets inside the heads of serial killers

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.060
to bring them to justice.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:56.730
The series premiere is directed by David Fincher,
virtually ensuring a dark, twisted kick-off

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:01.219
to a series that dives into the minds of the
most notorious psychopaths of the 20th century.

00:04:01.219 --> 00:04:04.290
Holt McCallany and Fringe's Anna Torv co-star.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.170
Get ready to binge on the insanity when the
first season hits on October 13.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:11.400
Voltron: Legendary Defender Season 4

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:15.359
Just two months after Season 3 hit Netflix,
the streaming service is bringing in the fourth

00:04:15.359 --> 00:04:19.019
season of its hit animated series Voltron:
Legendary Defender.

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:23.310
The same cast returns to voice the colorful
Paladins of Voltron, and the season four picks

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:27.590
up right where the third left off, with the
team of heroes working to stop their nemesis'

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:28.740
evil plan.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:32.300
Check in for more of the fast-paced action
on October 13.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.450
The Meyerowitz Stories

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:39.050
So far, Adam Sandler's Netflix films haven't
done much to impress either critics or audiences,

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:42.680
but that streak may end with The Meyerowitz
Stories, which sees Sandler headlining once

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:46.770
again with a supporting cast that includes
Dustin Hoffman, Emma Watson, and Ben Stiller,

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:47.770
to name a few.

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:51.240
With writer/director Noah Baumbach of The
Squid and the Whale at the helm, we're hoping

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.800
this installment in the Sandlerverse will
play the laughs more low key than some of

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:58.310
Sandler's previous films and deliver a compelling
story at the same time.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:02.050
So far, early critical response has been overwhelmingly
favorable.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:04.110
Check it out on October 13.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.310
The Babysitter

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:10.300
Netflix's original horror comedy The Babysitter
follows a 12-year-old boy named Cole who finds

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.870
out that his super hot babysitter happens
to be a satanic killer.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:18.639
And now that Cole knows her secret, he'll
have to kill or be killed to survive the night.

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:22.830
Directed by McG from a script by Brian Duffield,
The Babysitter premieres on Friday, October

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:23.919
13.

00:05:23.919 --> 00:05:26.330
Patton Oswalt: Annihilation

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:30.630
You've got to love Patton Oswalt, and the
affable everyman is back on October 17 with

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.510
a new one-hour stand-up special.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:36.780
In Annihilation, Oswalt gets more personal
than ever before as he works the pain and

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:40.530
loss of his wife's recent passing into a new,
intimate stand-up set.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:44.500
If you want to see Patton Oswalt as you've
never seen him, tune in for Annihilation and

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.720
be prepared for both laughs and tears along
the way.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.889
The Day I Met El Chapo: The Kate del Castillo
Story

00:05:50.889 --> 00:05:55.009
Told as a three-part mini-series, The Day
I Met El Chapo chronicles the fateful interview

00:05:55.009 --> 00:05:59.470
between one of history's most vicious drug
lords and A-list Mexican actress Kate del

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:00.470
Castillo.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:04.449
Castillo will star in the series as well as
produce, and the documentary will draw from

00:06:04.449 --> 00:06:08.539
real-life footage of the meeting and the planning
in the days and weeks leading up to the interview

00:06:08.539 --> 00:06:10.159
with the cartel kingpin.

00:06:10.159 --> 00:06:13.740
Get a closer look at the true story on October
20.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.909
Wheelman

00:06:14.909 --> 00:06:19.849
Strap in for high-stakes action and an adrenaline-filled
thrill ride when Wheelman drops on Netflix

00:06:19.849 --> 00:06:21.409
on October 20.

00:06:21.409 --> 00:06:25.169
Starring Frank Grillo as the wheelman in the
title, the story centers on a driver for a

00:06:25.169 --> 00:06:28.380
band of bank robbers who gets double crossed
on a job.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:32.129
With the lives of his family at stake, he'll
stop at nothing to find the truth and bring

00:06:32.129 --> 00:06:34.000
the backstabber to justice.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.350
It's kill or be killed, and hopefully this
feature film debut from writer/director Jeremy

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:43.509
Rush will deliver all the pulse-pounding action
promised in the Wheelman trailer.

00:06:43.509 --> 00:06:45.060
1922

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:49.499
Between his Castle Rock series, a Mist series,
The Dark Tower, Netflix's Gerald's Game, and

00:06:49.499 --> 00:06:54.759
— oh yeah — It, Stephen King is experiencing
a big-screen resurgence in a big way.

00:06:54.759 --> 00:06:59.550
King's next story to hit Netflix is 1922,
starring Thomas Jane as a rancher in the early

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:03.289
20th century who convinces his son to help
him murder his wife.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:07.629
If the film takes the same cues as the source
novella, 1922 will hopefully turn out to be

00:07:07.629 --> 00:07:11.199
a tense thriller fused with paranoia of the
worst kind.

00:07:11.199 --> 00:07:13.129
Check it out on October 20.

00:07:13.129 --> 00:07:14.949
Haters Back Off: Season 2

00:07:14.949 --> 00:07:18.919
Based on a YouTube channel called Miranda
Sings, created by Colleen Ballinger, Haters

00:07:18.919 --> 00:07:23.139
Back Off is a satirical look at YouTube fame
and everyone who wants a piece of that pie

00:07:23.139 --> 00:07:25.889
— with or without any discernible talent.

00:07:25.889 --> 00:07:30.919
This Netflix original first hit the streaming
service in 2016 and stars Ballinger in a continuation

00:07:30.919 --> 00:07:36.340
of her YouTube persona, Miranda Sings, a self-centered,
eccentric girl who thinks she's good at everything...when

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:37.340
she really isn't.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:40.300
Look for season 2 on October 20.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.479
One of Us

00:07:41.479 --> 00:07:46.159
This documentary certainly comes with an interesting
premise: it's about three Hasidic Jews living

00:07:46.159 --> 00:07:50.379
in a strict religious community in New York
who decide to leave that world behind.

00:07:50.379 --> 00:07:53.949
Abandoning everything they've ever known,
they face hate and violence from both the

00:07:53.949 --> 00:07:56.340
outside world and their former community.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.969
One of Us promises to be a slicing portrait
of religious intolerance and the struggle

00:07:59.969 --> 00:08:02.310
to live with all the cards stacked against
you.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.419
Look for it on October 20.

00:08:04.419 --> 00:08:06.379
Joan Didion: The Center Will Not Hold

00:08:06.379 --> 00:08:11.749
Novelist, journalist, and screenwriter Joan
Didion became the voice of the counter-culure

00:08:11.749 --> 00:08:16.030
through her stories and essays published throughout
the '60s and '70s, all the way up to the present

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.030
day.

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:20.810
The documentary The Center Will Not Hold travels
back in time across Didion's extraordinary

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:26.150
life to explore how a young writer became
a pop culture icon — and literary legend.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.659
Take the ride on October 27.

00:08:28.659 --> 00:08:30.539
Stranger Things: Season 2

00:08:30.539 --> 00:08:35.040
After a groundbreaking first season followed
by a painful year-long wait, Stranger Things

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:39.380
is finally back with season two, and things
promise to get even hairier in the Upside

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.000
Down this time around.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.220
Executive producer Shawn Levy told Variety
that the stakes are even higher in our next

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:49.640
visit to the town of Hawkins, as if we needed
any more incentive to tune in when Stranger

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:53.020
Things season two drops October 27.

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:57.380
Judah Friedlander: America is the Greatest
Country in the United States

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:02.160
With his deadpan delivery, ironic punchlines,
and big, shaggy beard, Judah Friedlander is

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:06.220
definitely a unique face in the stand-up world,
although most people likely know him best

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:08.810
from his role as Frank in 30 Rock.

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:12.990
Friedlander's new stand-up special, America
is the Greatest Country in the United States,

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:16.850
takes a stab at the American way of life,
lampooning everything from racism to foreign

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:17.850
policy.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:22.160
According to Friedland, the special will premiere
on Netflix on October 31, although Netflix

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.320
maintains that it will air on the 30th.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.440
Either way, it'll arrive just in time to help
you ease those late-night jitters after all

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:31.700
those horror movies you'll probably be watching
this month.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:32.700
New Movies

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:37.210
It wouldn't be a proper October without a
new lineup of horror and thriller movies,

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:42.050
and Netflix is bringing in some brand-new
shockers like 13 Demons, The Survivalist,

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:47.750
and Cult of Chucky, out October 3, followed
by 2017's cannibal thriller Raw the day after.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:51.420
For more down-to-earth thrills, this month
is seeing the addition of Blood Diamond and

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:55.580
Stanley Kubrick's Eyes Wide Shut, both of
which arrive October 1.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:59.730
Additionally, Donnie Darko arrives October
11th, and Quentin Tarantino's The Hateful

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:02.480
Eight is shooting for an October 25 premiere.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:07.390
For more casual viewing, look for the addition
of several cult classic comedies, like 1996's

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:11.510
Don’t Be a Menace to South Central While
Drinking Your Juice in the Hood.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.510
"Do.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:13.100
We.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:13.960
Have.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.240
A. Problem.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.340
Huh?"

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:21.410
On top of that, Netflix is bringing in Eagle
vs Shark, an offbeat indie comedy directed

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:26.190
by Taika Waititi and starring Jermaine Clement,
the same comedic duo who brought us What We

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.620
Do in the Shadows.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:33.010
Both films arrive October 1, along with I
Love You, Man, Tommy Boy, and both Miss Congeniality

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:34.010
movies.

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:37.600
Netflix's documentary game has been off the
charts lately, and October is set to continue

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:38.600
that trend.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:43.470
On October first, look for Generation Iron,
Ice Guardians, and Tokyo Idols.

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:47.760
Later in the month, get your music fix with
back-to-back biopics Mr. Dynamite: The Rise

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:53.780
of James Brown and Chris Brown: Welcome to
My Life, premiering on October 2 and 7, respectively.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:56.200
Finally, what's Halloween without family time?

00:10:56.200 --> 00:11:00.120
For the younger generation of trick-or-treaters,
Netflix is bringing on such family fare as

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:05.470
A Cinderella Story: Once Upon a Song, Charlie
and the Chocolate Factory, and 2017's Smurfs:

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:07.690
The Lost Village, to name a few.

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:09.000
New Television

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:12.890
Stranger Things may be the highlight of Netflix's
new series, but that doesn't mean there won't

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:16.550
be plenty of other new shows and seasons to
binge in the coming month.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:21.000
Highlights include season two of Cleverman
on October 1, season three of Schitt's Creek

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:25.380
on October 5, and the first season of the
serial adaptation of Stephen King's The Mist

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:30.680
on October 24, which follows new characters
caught in the same mysterious mist that terrorized

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:33.360
the cast of the 2007 film.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:37.870
Also arriving on October 24 are the first
two seasons of Wanted, the acclaimed Australian

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:42.970
drama series about two strangers who find
themselves drawn together during a murder

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:43.970
investigation.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.230
"He's never going to stop chasing us."

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:47.860
"There's no way out!"

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:49.089
Thanks for watching!

00:11:49.089 --> 00:11:51.490
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:53.990
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

